.TH LIBSTRARRAY_STRARRAY_POP 3 "2023-04-01" "libstrarray" "String Array Library"
.SH NAME
strarray_pop \- Remove and return the last element of a string array
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <libstrarray.h>
.sp
.B char*
.B strarray_pop(strarray* arr);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B strarray_pop
function removes and returns the last element of a string array. The
.B arr
argument is a pointer to a
.B strarray
structure representing the array.
The
.B strarray_pop
function returns the removed element, or NULL if the array is empty.
.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the
.B strarray_pop
function to remove and return the last element of a string array:
.nf
.B #include <libstrarray.h>
.B #include <stdio.h>
.sp
.B int main() {
.B   strarray arr;
.B   strarray_init(&arr);
.B   strarray_append(&arr, "Hello");
.B   strarray_append(&arr, "world");
.B   char* last_element = strarray_pop(&arr);
.B   printf("Last element: %s\n", last_element);
.B   // Free the allocated memory
.B   strarray_done(&arr);
.B   return 0;
.B }
.ne
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
